  "title": "Anthropic measures robot exposure across US work",
  "narration": "Anthropic just measured how much physical work robots can actually do today. The headline sounds wild: robots can perform 74 percent of physical tasks in the US, covering 34 percent of working hours. Add LLMs, and about 80 percent of job tasks are exposed to one or the other. But here’s the catch: robots are only cheaper than humans for 0.3 percent of tasks. At historical price declines, reaching 10 percent cost competitiveness could take around 40 years. Driving and warehouse jobs look highly exposed; nursing and repair work much less so.",
